# CODEOWNERS — who gets auto-requested as a reviewer for each area.
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Each line names the reviewing account as well as the team. A team owner only
# produces a review request when the team exists, has write access, and has a
# member other than the pull request author, so naming the account directly is
# what guarantees the request lands.

# Default owner — every path, unless overridden below.
*                               @The-Orange-Way/maintainers @Making-the-World-Orange

# Cryptographic primitives — require a crypto-aware reviewer.
/src/lib/                       @The-Orange-Way/maintainers @Making-the-World-Orange

# Vault context + unlock flow.
/src/context/                   @The-Orange-Way/maintainers @Making-the-World-Orange
/src/components/app/            @The-Orange-Way/maintainers @Making-the-World-Orange

# Supabase schema + RLS — migrations are the source of truth.
/supabase/                      @The-Orange-Way/maintainers @Making-the-World-Orange

# Docs — narrative surface of the project.
/README.md                      @The-Orange-Way/maintainers @Making-the-World-Orange
/CONTRIBUTING.md                @The-Orange-Way/maintainers @Making-the-World-Orange
/SECURITY.md                    @The-Orange-Way/maintainers @Making-the-World-Orange
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md             @The-Orange-Way/maintainers @Making-the-World-Orange

# GitHub workflows + community health files.
/.github/                       @The-Orange-Way/maintainers @Making-the-World-Orange
